/-!
# glibc's `libm.so.6` against the pinned `math.h`: classification and rows

**The file** (`F`): glibc 2.36 `libm.so.6` of Debian 12 `libc6` 2.36-9+deb12u14 (amd64),
`examples/elf/pinned/glibc-2.36-libm.so.6` (SHA-256 `7f2ca87f…b271b4e7`,
`Elf.Staged.Pinned.GlibcLibm236`): the `libm.so.6` of the image
`silkeh/clang@sha256:3914c93a…` whose `math.h` is the pinned import `Pinned.glibcMath`
(`examples/headers/clang/glibc-math.prov`). Header and binary are one glibc build.

**The functions**: the 288 functions of `glibcMath` that `sysvScalar` can claim
(`Conformance.glibcMath_coverage_sysvScalar`: float and double in SSE registers; the 150
`long double` ones are refused, X87 class). **Classification** (`classes`, generated by
`scripts/libm-rows/gen.py`, every entry checked in the kernel, `Thms.classes_*`): ld.so's
versioned lookup of each function's **default version** (`name@@VER`, what a program linked
against this file requests) in `.dynsym`:

| class | count | what a row can say |
|---|---|---|
| plain `STT_FUNC` | 121 | `CodeOf` can hold: a row is possible |
| `STT_GNU_IFUNC` | 25 | refused: `CodeOf` is false for every code (`not_codeOf_ifunc`); the resolver picks the code at load time |
| absent | 142 | `Absent`: no symbol of that name in any table (`__acos`, `__isinf`, …: glibc's `__MATHCALL` internal names, and the `is*` helpers that live in `libc.so.6`) |

18 of the 146 present functions have a default version other than `GLIBC_2.2.5` (`exp`, `log`,
`pow`, `exp2`, `log2` at `GLIBC_2.29`, `expf`, `logf`, … at `GLIBC_2.27`, `lgamma` at
`GLIBC_2.23`, `hypot` at `GLIBC_2.35`, …); 14 also keep a compat (`@`) version. The lookup is the
versioned one for every function (`Class.binding`); an unversioned reference to a symbol whose
version index is 3 or more is undetermined in the lookup model (`File.checkMatch`), so no row
uses it.

**The file refuses `Untouched`** (`Thms.not_untouched`): its dynamic relocations include 21
`R_X86_64_IRELATIVE` (the IFUNC slots of `libm` itself), which make ld.so run resolver code.
`Untouched` refuses every file with one, so **`AbiConforms` is false for every function of this
file** (`Thms.not_abiConforms`). The rows therefore state the file facts and the conformance of
the code at every load base as separate statements, not the `abi_conforms` shape.

**Rows** (plain functions whose code the generator's sweep finds free of RIP-relative operands,
`%fs`, calls, branches out of the symbol, indirect branches, VEX/EVEX, BMI and x87 forms, and
whose every instruction `Mach.str9L` steps; the unverified per-function sweep is
`examples/elf/libm-rows/classification.txt`). Every file fact is PROVED: `CodeOf` (versioned
lookup, `STT_FUNC`, bytes, image), `Placement F 0`, `Declares` through a header text whose
prototypes are checked equal to `Pinned.glibcMath`'s (`Thms.hdr_agrees`), hence
`DeclaresImport … glibcMath` (`Thms.declares_iff`). Conformance on `mach` under `abi`:

| function | prototype | spec | conformance at every load base |
|---|---|---|---|
| `lrint`, `llrint` | `long (double)` (`long long`: same lowering) | `Lrint.toLong` | **PROVED** (`Thms.lrint_conforms`, `llrint_conforms`) |
| `lrintf`, `llrintf` | `long (float)` | `toLongF` (x86 SSE `toInt`, binary32) | open (`Task.libm_lrintf`, `libm_llrintf`) |
| `round` | `double (double)` | `roundAway`: `roundToIntegral`, ties away | open (`Task.libm_round`) |
| `fmax`, `fmin` | `double (double, double)` | `abiPure` | open (`Task.libm_fmax`, `libm_fmin`), frame 8 (a red-zone store) |
| `__fpclassify`, `__signbit`, `__finite`, `finite` | `int (double)` | `abiPure` | open (`Task.libm_fpclassify`, `libm_signbit`, `libm_finiteInternal`, `libm_finite`) |

`fmax`/`fmin` have no value spec: glibc's code returns `maxsd`'s second operand for equal
operands, so `fmax(+0, -0)` is `-0`, while `Numeric.Float`'s `minNum` rule picks `+0`; C and IEEE
754-2008 `maxNum` leave the sign of that zero open, so the value is a relation, not one of the
profile's functions. The classification functions return glibc's `FP_*` values and bit masks,
which are no `Numeric.Float` operation. No row carries an algorithmic contract.

**Not stated** (model gaps and exclusions, in the report): `lround`, `llround` (`bts`) and
`__issignaling` (`btc`) are stuck on `Str9L`, so their rows would be false on the model;
`copysign` (`movq xmm, [rip+d]`) likewise; `fabs`, `fabsf`, `copysignf` read a `.rodata` mask,
and `Placed.data` grants the callee's data **execute** permission only (`Ext.Loaded`), so an
admitted state with an execute-only data page faults on the load: false as defined; functions
reaching `errno` through `%fs` and a `TPOFF64`-relocated GOT slot (`fdim`, `__iseqsig`, …),
calling or tail-calling other code (PLT or internal), or using x87 are out of this model's scope.

**Limits.** The rows are on a machine **model** (`Mach.str9L FeatureSet.baseline64
Features.sseExts`); `Faithful` of a reference machine to it is not proved, so nothing here is a
claim about hardware, and the rows cover the functions listed, not the library: the other
plain functions are unaudited on this machine. The ABI is the **default-environment subset**
`sysvScalar.defaultEnv` (named, not unfolded: entry MXCSR control bits `0x1F80`, status flags
free); the value specs (`Lrint.toLong`, `toLongF`, `roundAway`) read the entry MXCSR only through
`MXCSR.profile` and `MXCSR.rounding`, i.e. its control bits (`Lrint.toLong_mask`). The row code
has no VEX/EVEX or BMI form (the sweep; `Mach.str9L` on `baseline64` has no step at such a form
anyway), no `%fs` access (no thread-pointer assumption is needed), no call through the PLT, no
`rdssp`, and `ret` is modelled without a shadow stack: the rows are about processes without user
shadow stacks.
-/

@[expose] public section

namespace Silmaril.Elf.Abi.Libm

open Silmaril.Elf
open Silmaril.Machine.Abi.Conformance
open Silmaril.X86.Link (Blob)
open Silmaril.X86 (Word Byte)

/-- The pinned file. -/
noncomputable abbrev F : Blob := Silmaril.Elf.Staged.Pinned.GlibcLibm236.F

/-- Its parse (`Pinned.GlibcLibm236.parses`). -/
abbrev A0 : File :=
  Silmaril.Elf.Staged.Pinned.GlibcLibm236.L.assemble Silmaril.Elf.Staged.Pinned.GlibcLibm236.bodies
    Silmaril.Elf.Staged.Pinned.GlibcLibm236.ld

/-! ## The classification -/

/-- How a classified function is looked up: ld.so's lookup in `.dynsym` of its default
version. -/
def Class.binding : Class → Binding
  | .plain v .. | .ifunc v .. => .dynsym (some v)
  | .absent => .dynsym none

/-- Entry `i` of `.dynsym` is an `STT_FUNC` named `f`. -/
def funcSymB (A : File) (i : Nat) (f : String) : Bool :=
  match (A.symbols .dynsym)[i]? with
  | some s => s.name == nameOf f && s.kind == 2
  | none => false

/-- No table has a defined symbol named `f` (any type, any version). -/
def absentB (A : File) (f : String) : Bool :=
  [Table.symtab, .dynsym].all fun t => (A.symbols t).all fun s =>
    s.name != nameOf f || s.raw.sectionIndex == 0

/-- **The class is what the parse `A` says**: the versioned lookup finds the plain definition
(index, value, size) and the entry is an `STT_FUNC` named `f`; or it finds an IFUNC definition
at the index; or no table defines `f`. -/
def Class.check (A : File) (f : String) : Class → Bool
  | .plain v i val sz =>
    A.select ((Binding.dynsym (some v)).sel f) == some (some ⟨i, val, sz, false, false⟩) &&
      funcSymB A i f
  | .ifunc v i =>
    match A.select ((Binding.dynsym (some v)).sel f) with
    | some (some d) => d.index == i && d.ifunc
    | _ => false
  | .absent => absentB A f

/-- **What a class says of the file**: a plain function found at its value and size and
named in an `STT_FUNC` entry; an IFUNC, of which no code is the function (`CodeOf` refuses
it); or absent from every table. -/
def Class.Holds (F : Blob) (f : String) : Class → Prop
  | .plain v i val sz =>
    Lookup F ((Binding.dynsym (some v)).sel f) (some ⟨i, val, sz, false, false⟩) ∧
      ∃ s, SymbolAt F .dynsym i s ∧ s.name = nameOf f ∧ s.kind = 2
  | .ifunc v _ => ∀ c, ¬ CodeOf F (.dynsym (some v)) f c
  | .absent => Absent F f

def Class.isPlain : Class → Bool | .plain .. => true | _ => false
def Class.isIfunc : Class → Bool | .ifunc .. => true | _ => false
def Class.isAbsent : Class → Bool | .absent => true | _ => false

/-- The default version of a present function, if it is not `GLIBC_2.2.5`. -/
def Class.laterVersion : Class → Bool
  | .plain v .. | .ifunc v .. => v != v2_2_5
  | .absent => false

/-! ## The rows -/

/-- The prototypes of the rows, as a header text. Not trusted: `Thms.hdr_agrees` checks that
every row function's prototype here **is** `Pinned.glibcMath`'s (the clang import of the pinned
`math.h`), and `Thms.declares_iff` that `Declares` through it is `DeclaresImport` of the
import. -/
def hdr : HeaderSrc := ⟨[("math.h", "extern int __fpclassify (double __value);
extern int __signbit (double __value);
extern int __finite (double __value);
extern int finite (double __value);
extern double round (double __x);
extern long int lrint (double __x);
extern long long int llrint (double __x);
extern long int lrintf (float __x);
extern long long int llrintf (float __x);
extern double fmax (double __x, double __y);
extern double fmin (double __x, double __y);
")], "math.h"⟩

/-- The row functions. -/
def rowNames : List String :=
  ["__fpclassify", "__signbit", "__finite", "finite", "round", "lrint", "llrint", "lrintf",
    "llrintf", "fmax", "fmin"]

/-- The image of the file: its four `PT_LOAD` ranges (`Thms.image_eq`). -/
def image : List (Word × Nat) :=
  [(0, 62912), (65536, 472033), (540672, 367252), (912696, 984)]

/-- A function's code: its bytes at its `st_value`, entered at offset 0, extent `st_size`, no
data, the file's image. -/
def codeAt (value : Nat) (bytes : List Byte) : Code :=
  ⟨BitVec.ofNat 64 value, bytes, 0, bytes.length, [], image⟩

def lrintCode : Code := codeAt 0x32760 lrintBytes
def llrintCode : Code := codeAt 0x32760 llrintBytes
def lrintfCode : Code := codeAt 0x415d0 lrintfBytes
def llrintfCode : Code := codeAt 0x415d0 llrintfBytes
def roundCode : Code := codeAt 0x311c0 roundBytes
def fmaxCode : Code := codeAt 0x38e30 fmaxBytes
def fminCode : Code := codeAt 0x38e70 fminBytes
def fpclassifyCode : Code := codeAt 0x30bf0 fpclassifyBytes
def signbitCode : Code := codeAt 0x32c70 signbitBytes
def finiteInternalCode : Code := codeAt 0x32980 finiteInternalBytes
def finiteCode : Code := codeAt 0x32980 finiteBytes

/-- The ABI of the rows, by name: the default-environment subset of `sysvScalar`. -/
abbrev abi : AbiDef := sysvScalar.defaultEnv

/-- The machine of the rows. -/
abbrev mach : Mach := Silmaril.Machine.Abi.Conformance.Sse.Lrint.mach

open Silmaril.Machine.Abi.SystemV.Scalar (Proto)

/-- `int (double)`. -/
def dInt : Proto := ⟨[.scalar .double], some (.scalar .int32), by decide⟩
/-- `double (double)`. -/
def dDouble : Proto := ⟨[.scalar .double], some (.scalar .double), by decide⟩
/-- `double (double, double)`. -/
def ddDouble : Proto := ⟨[.scalar .double, .scalar .double], some (.scalar .double), by decide⟩
/-- `long (float)` (and `long long (float)`). -/
def fLong : Proto := ⟨[.scalar .float], some (.scalar .int64), by decide⟩

/-- binary32 to a signed 64-bit integer as `cvtss2si` computes it under MXCSR `m`. -/
def toLongF (m : BitVec 32) (a : BitVec 32) : BitVec 64 :=
  (Silmaril.X86.Float.Scalar.toInt ⟨m⟩ .single .w64 (⟨m⟩ : Silmaril.X86.Float.MXCSR).rounding
    a).value

/-- `lrintf`'s spec: every call admitted, nothing written, the result `toLongF` of the entry
MXCSR. -/
def lrintfSpec : CallSpec abi.V fLong where
  pre _ _ := True
  post a s r _ := r = toLongF s.mxcsr a.1

/-- **binary64 `round`**: IEEE 754-2019 §5.9 `roundToIntegralTiesToAway` by `Numeric.Float`'s
x86 SSE profile of MXCSR `m` (C17 7.12.9.6: halfway cases away from zero, whatever the current
direction). -/
def roundAway (m : BitVec 32) (a : BitVec 64) : BitVec 64 :=
  ((⟨m⟩ : Silmaril.X86.Float.MXCSR).profile.roundToIntegral .binary64 .nearestTiesToAway false
    a).value

/-- `round`'s spec: every call admitted, nothing written, the result `roundAway` of the entry
MXCSR. -/
def roundSpec : CallSpec abi.V dDouble where
  pre _ _ := True
  post a s r _ := r = roundAway s.mxcsr a.1

/-- **Open**: `lrintf` (`cvtss2si %xmm0, %rax; ret`) conforms at every load base. -/
def Task.libm_lrintf : Prop :=
  ∀ base, Placement F base → Conforms abi mach .total hdr "lrintf" fLong (lrintfCode.rebase base) 0
    lrintfSpec
/-- **Open**: `llrintf` (the same code). -/
def Task.libm_llrintf : Prop :=
  ∀ base, Placement F base →
    Conforms abi mach .total hdr "llrintf" fLong (llrintfCode.rebase base) 0 lrintfSpec
/-- **Open**: `round` conforms at every load base, with the result `roundAway`. -/
def Task.libm_round : Prop :=
  ∀ base, Placement F base → Conforms abi mach .total hdr "round" dDouble (roundCode.rebase base) 0
    roundSpec
/-- **Open**: `fmax` conforms (ABI only) at every load base, with an 8-byte frame (its store
below `%rsp`). -/
def Task.libm_fmax : Prop :=
  ∀ base, Placement F base → Conforms abi mach .total hdr "fmax" ddDouble (fmaxCode.rebase base) 8
    (CallSpec.abiPure _ _)
/-- **Open**: `fmin`, as `fmax`. -/
def Task.libm_fmin : Prop :=
  ∀ base, Placement F base → Conforms abi mach .total hdr "fmin" ddDouble (fminCode.rebase base) 8
    (CallSpec.abiPure _ _)
/-- **Open**: `__fpclassify` conforms (ABI only) at every load base. -/
def Task.libm_fpclassify : Prop :=
  ∀ base, Placement F base →
    Conforms abi mach .total hdr "__fpclassify" dInt (fpclassifyCode.rebase base) 0
      (CallSpec.abiPure _ _)
/-- **Open**: `__signbit` conforms (ABI only) at every load base. -/
def Task.libm_signbit : Prop :=
  ∀ base, Placement F base →
    Conforms abi mach .total hdr "__signbit" dInt (signbitCode.rebase base) 0
      (CallSpec.abiPure _ _)
/-- **Open**: `__finite` conforms (ABI only) at every load base. -/
def Task.libm_finiteInternal : Prop :=
  ∀ base, Placement F base →
    Conforms abi mach .total hdr "__finite" dInt (finiteInternalCode.rebase base) 0 (CallSpec.abiPure _ _)
/-- **Open**: `finite` (the same code as `__finite`). -/
def Task.libm_finite : Prop :=
  ∀ base, Placement F base →
    Conforms abi mach .total hdr "finite" dInt (finiteCode.rebase base) 0 (CallSpec.abiPure _ _)

end Silmaril.Elf.Abi.Libm

